  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &apos;Food Assistance, WASH, and Protection for IDPs affected by M23 conflict in North Kivu&apos; in The Democratic Republic of Congo implemented by Oxfam through FOPAC-NK partner has reached 30,865 IDPs in the camps at Lushagala and Mweso. Through this Acute Crisis Response, affected communities accessed clean water, food, protection services and safe sanitation infrastructure. Gender and protection were mainstreamed throughout the intervention, reducing the vulnerability of children and women..  OUTCOME: Objective/Outcome 1: Improved access to and use of safe, dignified and gender-sensitive water and hygiene services for 24,000 displaced people in the Lushagala site..  SPECIFIC OUTCOME:</narrative>
  </description>
